  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">WHO - NIH/HMIS st&#xf6;d</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">WHO - NIH/HMIS support</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Denna insats skall ge finansiellt st&#xf6;d till WHO Somalia och har som huvudsyfte att med WHO:s tekniska expertis st&#xf6;dja tv&#xe5; andra svenska insatser som implementeras i Somalia, n&#xe4;mligen utvecklandet av en Somalisk Folkh&#xe4;lsomyndighet som sker i ett samarbete med den svenska folkh&#xe4;lsomyndigheten och att digitalisera Somalias h&#xe4;lsohanteringsinformationssystem som sker genom ett samarbete med Stockholms Universitet/SPIDER. Insatsen bygger dels p&#xe5; de arbetsplaner som WHO har &#xf6;verenskommit med folkh&#xe4;lsomyndigheten och med Stockholms universitet/SPIDER och dels p&#xe5; de arbetsbeskrivningar som tagits fram f&#xf6;r de tv&#xe5; experter som kommer st&#xf6;dja implementeringen.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This contribution will provide financial support to WHO Somalia to allow WHO to dedicate technical expertise two other Swedish initiatives implemented in Somalia and has as its main purpose to support two other Swedish initiatives implemented in Somalia, namely the development of a Somali Public Health Agency in collaboration with the Swedish Public Health Agency and to digitilize Somalia&apos;s health management information system which takes place through a collaboration with Stockholm University / SPIDER. The contribution is based on both the work plans that the WHO has agreed with the public health authority and with Stockholm University / SPIDER and also on the job descriptions prepared for the two experts WHO will provide to support the implementation.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of this contribution is to strengthening the health system
in Somalia by supporting the building and strengthening of essential public health functions.

The specific objective of the intervention is to:

1) Support the establishment of an independent National Institute for Health (NIH) in Somalia, and;

2) Strengthening the Health  Management Information System (HMIS) in pilot locations across Somalia, as well as working towards the development of an integrated disease surveillance and response system in Somalia.</narrative>
  </description>
